import QOU.Descartes.GroundRing

/-!
# Markov-axiom recursive ascent for the Jones–Markov trace

Lean scaffold for the production recursive-ascent algorithm
implemented in `folio-assistant/computations/markov_peel.py`
([#508](https://github.com/litlfred/qou/issues/508) /
[PR #516](https://github.com/litlfred/qou/pull/516)).

The Python production path evaluates `tr_M(β)` for atomic braids
by peeling the topmost generator via the Markov axiom

  tr_M^{(n)}(x · σ_{n−1}) = z · tr_M^{(n−1)}(x)    ∀ x ∈ H_{n−1}(q)

recursing down `H_n ⊃ H_{n−1} ⊃ … ⊃ H_1`.  At every step the
Hecke quadratic σ_i² = (q − q⁻¹)·σ_i + 1 produces a binary
branching, but the recursion terminates in time bounded by the
braid length.

This file states the **abstract** typeclass `MarkovTrace`
encoding the three defining axioms (M1 cyclicity, M2 Markov,
M3 unit) over an arbitrary Hecke-like algebra type, plus the
key reference proposition `markov_pair_z2`
([prop:markov-pair-z2](#prop:markov-pair-z2)).

The recursive evaluator `markov_peel` itself is left as a
`noncomputable` declaration with a `sorry` carrying a
bibliographic citation per CLAUDE.md §1; concrete computational
witnesses live in `markov-peel-atomic-tr-m.witness.json` and the
Python implementation, both verified against
`atomic-tr-m-mpfr-50dps.witness.json` (Hoefsmit + Wenzl bridge).

## Main definitions

- `MarkovTrace H R` — typeclass: a Markov trace on `H` valued in `R`
- `markov_pair_z2` — the trace-pair identity `tr_M(σ_i · σ_j) = z²`
  for the simplest non-trivial case (which the production
  `tr_M_sigma_pair_is_z²` test verifies).

## References

- [jones1987] V.F.R. Jones, *Hecke algebra representations of braid
  groups and link polynomials*, Annals of Math. 126 (1987), 335–388.
  <https://doi.org/10.2307/1971403>
- [kassel2008] C. Kassel, V. Turaev, *Braid groups*, Springer GTM 247.
  <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-0-387-68548-9>
-/

namespace QOU.Interactions

open QOU.Descartes

/-! ## §1  Abstract Markov trace -/

/-- A Markov-trace structure on a multiplicative algebra `H`
    valued in a commutative ring `R`.  Encodes the three defining
    axioms of the canonical Jones-Markov trace:

    * **(M1)** Cyclicity:   `tr (a * b) = tr (b * a)`
    * **(M2)** Markov peel: `tr (x * σ_{n-1}) = z * tr x`  whenever
      `x` lies in the rank-`(n-1)` subalgebra generated by
      `σ_0, ..., σ_{n-2}`.
    * **(M3)** Unit:        `tr 1 = 1`

    `top` selects the topmost generator at strand-count `n`;
    `belowTop x` predicts whether `x` lives in the rank-`(n-1)`
    subalgebra.  The (M2) axiom is conditional on `belowTop`. -/
class MarkovTrace (H : Type*) [Mul H] [One H] (R : Type*) [CommRing R] where
  /-- The trace function. -/
  tr : H → R
  /-- The Markov parameter `z = 1 / (q^½ + q^{-½})`. -/
  z : R
  /-- Topmost-generator selector at strand-count `n`. -/
  top : Nat → H
  /-- Rank predicate: `belowTop n x` iff `x ∈ H_{n-1}` (no `σ_{n-1}`). -/
  belowTop : Nat → H → Prop
  /-- (M1) Cyclicity. -/
  cyclic : ∀ a b : H, tr (a * b) = tr (b * a)
  /-- (M3) Unit. -/
  unit_one : tr (1 : H) = 1
  /-- (M2) Markov peel.  For any `x` in the rank-`(n-1)` subalgebra,
      multiplying by the topmost generator `σ_{n-1}` factors a `z`
      out of the trace. -/
  markov : ∀ (n : Nat) (x : H), belowTop n x → tr (x * top n) = z * tr x

/-! ## §2  Reference identity — `prop:markov-pair-z2` -/

/-- `prop:markov-pair-z2`: For non-adjacent generators
    `σ_i, σ_j` (`|i − j| ≥ 2`), the Markov trace of their product
    is `z²`.

    This is the simplest non-trivial application of the Markov
    axiom: by far-commutativity `σ_i σ_j = σ_j σ_i`, then
    cyclicity, then two consecutive Markov peels.  The Python
    production test `test_tr_M_sigma_pair_is_z_squared` verifies
    it numerically.

    The Lean formalization at the typeclass level requires
    additional hypotheses (`σ_i, σ_j` are topmost at successive
    strand counts; far-commutativity holds in `H`); these are
    bundled below as a single `belowTop` chain. -/
theorem markov_pair_z2
    {H : Type*} [Mul H] [One H] [Mul.assoc : Std.Associative (· * · : H → H → H)]
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [tr : MarkovTrace H R]
    (n : Nat) (x : H)
    (h_below_n : tr.belowTop n x)
    (h_below_pred : tr.belowTop (n - 1) x) :
    tr.tr (x * tr.top n * tr.top (n - 1)) = tr.z ^ 2 * tr.tr x := by
  -- Ref: [jones1987] https://doi.org/10.2307/1971403
  -- Ref: [manuscript] prop:markov-pair-z2 (QOU narrative)
  sorry

/-! ## §3  Recursive-ascent evaluator (scaffold) -/

/-- Recursive Markov-axiom evaluator.

    Production-side analogue of
    [`markov_peel.tr_M_atomic`](https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/main/folio-assistant/computations/markov_peel.py).
    Takes a Hecke-algebra element `x` and a strand count `n`,
    peels the topmost generator via (M2) when present, and
    recurses on the residue.  The base case is `tr_M^{(1)}(1) = 1`.

    Currently a `noncomputable` declaration whose body is the
    abstract trace — concrete recursion is supplied by the
    Python production path (verified against the Hoefsmit + Wenzl
    bridge to ~1e-15) and by future concrete `MarkovTrace`
    instances on `HeckeNF`. -/
noncomputable def markov_peel
    {H : Type*} [Mul H] [One H]
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [tr : MarkovTrace H R]
    (_n : Nat) (x : H) : R :=
  tr.tr x

end QOU.Interactions
